# Store every text file with LF endings and check it out that way on
# every platform. The tree is all text today; `text=auto` rather than a
# bare `text` keeps that from mangling a binary asset added later.
#
# `eol=lf` is not cosmetic here. The `.stderr` fixtures under `ui/` and
# `ui-toml/` are compared byte-for-byte against the driver's output,
# which is LF; a CRLF working tree would fail every UI test.
* text=auto eol=lf
